#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# throw

#% text
# `throw(v)` gives `failure(thrown, v)` and `throw(v, tag)` gives `failure(thrown, v, tag)`. Like every failure it ends blocks and loops and passes through strict calls, until a `catch` takes its value.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
throw(1)
#% output
#! failure(thrown, 1)

#% cell
catch({ print("before"); throw(7); print("never") })
#% output
#| before
#= 7

#% cell
catch(throw(a, done), done)
#% output
#= a

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `catch`, `is_failure`, `drop_failures`
